  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will continue\nto build eastward across northern and central Nevada. The result\nof increasing heights will be a warming trend that will expand\nsouth and east this afternoon. High temperatures throughout \nNorthern and Central Nevada today will be about ten degrees above\nseasonal values with readings in the 80s. Overnight lows will be\nin the 40s \n\nThe upper ridge axis will be over southern Nevada and southwest \nUtah Friday. This upper-level area of high pressure will remain \nacross the Desert Southwest this weekend. High temperatures each \nafternoon Friday through Sunday will be around fifteen degrees \nabove normal for this time of year. Near record warmth is \nanticipated in Elko, Ely, and Tonopah Friday afternoon. Near \nrecord warmth is expected in Elko, Winnemucca, and Ely Saturday \nafternoon. Near record warmth is anticipated in Elko and Ely \nSunday afternoon. \n\nA weak trough of low pressure will pass eastward across the \nSilver State Monday. This will result in a downward temperature \ntrend and possibly a light shower or two. Be that as it may, high \ntemperatures will remain well above seasonal values both Monday \nafternoon and Tuesday afternoon.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No adjustments were made to the\nNBM model output. High forecast confidence regarding a warming \ntrend this afternoon. High forecast confidence in unseasonably \nwarm weather Friday through Sunday. Moderate forecast confidence \nregarding near record warmth in most of northern and central \nNevada both Friday afternoon and Saturday afternoon. Moderate \nforecast confidence in near record warmth in parts of northern and\ncentral Nevada Sunday afternoon.",
